# Fingerprints of gitleaks findings reviewed and confirmed to be false positives.
#
# Format: <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>. Fingerprints pin one specific occurrence rather than
# disabling a rule, so a genuine key committed elsewhere, or later in this same file, is still
# caught. Each entry needs a reason.
#
# Note these reference historical commits on purpose: the CI job scans history, not just the
# working tree, so a finding stays reported even after the line is changed. That is the correct
# behaviour for secret scanning, since anything once committed remains retrievable.

